      "amount": "2 tablespoons"
    },
    {
      "name": "olive oil",
      "amount": "2 tablespoons"
    },
    {
      "name": "salt",
      "amount": "1 teaspoon"
    },
    {
      "name": "black pepper",
      "amount": "1 teaspoon"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large cazuela over medium high heat.",
    "Add the beef short ribs and cook until browned on all sides, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the chopped onions and cook until they are translucent, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and cook for 1 minute, until fragrant.",
    "Add the red wine, beef broth, tomato paste, salt, and black pepper, and stir to combine.",
    "Bring the stew to a boil, then reduce the heat to low and simmer, covered, for 2 1/2 hours.",
    "Add the chopped perilla leaves to the stew and cook for an additional 30 minutes, until the leaves are wilted.",
    "Serve the stew hot, garnished with additional perilla leaves if desired."
  ],
